  "_disclaimer": "SIMULATED DEMONSTRATION WEIGHTS -- NOT CLINICAL GUIDELINES. These point values express relative concern for a prototype demonstration. They are not derived from outcome data and carry no clinical authority.",
  "_design_note": "Weights are deliberately readable. A judge should be able to open this file and see exactly why a patient scored what they scored. That transparency is the reason we chose a weighted engine over a trained model on synthetic data.",
  "_domains": "Every signal belongs to a clinical domain. Domains are CAPPED, because correlated findings must not stack. A breathless patient may trip seven separate respiratory signals; that is one clinical problem, not seven. Without caps, an asthma exacerbation scores the same as a cardiac arrest.",
